WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.980
Mice born without one chloride channel have normal-looking pacemaker cells in the

2
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.060
gut but no electrical slow waves.

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.740
What does that channel do?

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.860
The gut wall keeps its own time.

5
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.580
The beat comes from branched cells between the muscle layers, the interstitial cells

6
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.200
of Cajal, or ICC.

7
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:26.013
Record from a gut smooth muscle cell and you see slow waves, which are rhythmic

8
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:27.773
depolarizations that last seconds.

9
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:31.773
In the human stomach, pacemaker cells generate about 3 a minute.

10
00:00:32.573 --> 00:00:37.213
Isolated ICC show this rhythm, but isolated smooth muscle cells do not typically

11
00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:42.473
show it. In paired recordings from mouse gut muscle, the waves were larger in ICC.

12
00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:47.493
They reached the muscle passively, shrinking as they spread, so smooth muscle cannot

13
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:48.493
regenerate them.

14
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:53.957
A slow wave is not an action potential, and it sets when the muscle can contract.

15
00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:59.077
A contraction follows only when a wave carries the muscle past threshold for calcium

16
00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:01.877
entry. Think of a metronome and a pianist.

17
00:01:02.337 --> 00:01:06.657
The metronome fixes the beat, and the pianist decides how loud each note is.

18
00:01:07.477 --> 00:01:12.597
Excitatory and inhibitory neurons, and hormones, set how strongly each wave couples

19
00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:13.597
to contraction.

20
00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:19.557
Small-intestinal muscle from Kit-mutant mice, with few myenteric ICC, lacked the

21
00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:21.157
slow waves of wild-type siblings.

22
00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:26.897
Mice lacking ANO1 failed to develop slow waves, yet their ICC networks looked

23
00:01:26.897 --> 00:01:31.357
normal. So a calcium-activated chloride current is necessary for the rhythm,

24
00:01:31.697 --> 00:01:33.137
separately from building the network.

25
00:01:33.797 --> 00:01:36.717
It does not show that ANO1 is the whole pacemaker.

26
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:41.017
It describes neonatal mice, not adults or any human disorder.

27
00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.850
The enteric nervous system is the network of neurons in the gut wall.

28
00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:51.350
The myenteric plexus, between the circular and longitudinal muscle layers, mainly

29
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.370
controls movement.

30
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.790
In 1899, Bayliss and Starling recorded loops of small intestine in anesthetized

31
00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:04.450
dogs. Distension of the wall caused contraction on the oral side and relaxation on

32
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.910
the anal side, driving contents anally.

33
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.570
The response persisted after the extrinsic nerves were cut, but was lost when

34
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.390
conduction within the wall was blocked.

35
00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:16.953
So the gut splits the work.

36
00:02:17.473 --> 00:02:20.913
ICC keep the beat, and the beat sets when the muscle can contract.

37
00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:25.353
Neurons and hormones set how strongly each wave couples to contraction.

38
00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:29.793
Keep this rule. Slow waves mainly set the timing of contraction.
